──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
• Composition : full-screen tour spotlight — a dimming scrim with a transparent rounded spotlight
                cutout, a glowing spotlight ring, and a floating tooltip card (close button, step
                counter, step title + description, Skip / Back / Next|Get Started! controls, progress
                dots). Every region of TourOverlay.tsx is reproduced.
• Geometry    : faithful port of the web `spotlight` (target + 6pt padding) and `getTooltipPosition`
                (16pt gap off the chosen edge, 16pt viewport margin, 72pt bottom-safe inset, 360pt max
                width) — all four placements (top/bottom/left/right) + on-screen clamping. Extracted to
                the pure `TourGeometry` so the arithmetic is unit-tested against the exact web numbers.
• Phases      : inactive (web `if (!targetRect) return null` → renders nothing, the surface's only
                "no content" branch, reproduced exactly — not a hidden section of a visible panel) and
                active, with the active sub-branches: first step (no Back) / middle (Back + Next) /
                last + single (Back? + Get Started!, no trailing arrow), the four placements, the
                reduce-motion toggle, and the progress dots. (This surface issues NO query, so the
                data-centric loading/empty/error/stale/offline axes do not apply; nothing was dropped —
                every branch that exists in the web source is reproduced.)
• Motion      : the bound `useMotionPreference().reduce` flag (carried in the input snapshot, P1/S8 —
                NOT read from the environment) gates both the inter-step spotlight animation and the
                tooltip fade/slide-in entrance, reproducing the web `reduce ? '' : 'transition-all' /
                'animate-in …'` switch.
• onNext/onPrev/onSkip : forwarded through the P1/S8 state-holder seam (TourOverlaySource.next/prev/skip);
                the view issues no HTTP and owns no tour state. Scrim tap + close button + Skip control
                all dismiss (web overlay onClick + close + skip).
• i18n        : 100% via the P1/S10 facade (TourStrings, table "TourOverlay"); zero English literals in
                Swift beyond the web-default fallbacks. Keys: tour.dialogLabel, tour.stepCounter,
                tour.close, tour.skip, tour.prev, tour.finish, tour.next (the tour step title/description
                are dynamic content from the tour definition, localized upstream — passed through).
• Telemetry   : P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted exactly once with surface slug "TourOverlay", deferred until
                the overlay is actually presented (active) — mirrors the web `data-tour-active` marker.
• a11y        : VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (close, skip, back, next); the tooltip is a
                contained dialog labeled "Tour step N of M" (web role=dialog / aria-modal=false); an
                `.escape` accessibility action dismisses; spotlight ring + dots are decorative-hidden;
                Dynamic Type via Font.TS roles; reduce-motion respected.

